#
# (a) fresh directory per job: march() uses tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="m_<tag>_", dir=WORK) and
#     solve() uses tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="s_<k>_", dir=WORK); the CNF, the LRAT proof and the
#     solver stdout of a job live only in that directory and cake_lpr is run on exactly those two
#     files; the directory is removed after the record is written. No shared s_k names (AUDIT RISK-3b). OK.
# (b) atomic writes: finalize() writes leaves.icnf and open.icnf with tempfile.mkstemp in the
#     output directory, then os.replace() into place (AUDIT RISK-1). Every line is written as
#     "a l1 .. lk 0\n". OK.
# (c) first leaves.jsonl record: when leaves.jsonl does not exist it writes
#     {"case": --name, "case_sha256": sha256 of the case CNF} before anything else. OK
#     (I always start from an empty output directory, so no stale records: AUDIT RISK-3c).
# Also checked:
# - BUG-1: a leaf enters leaves.icnf only if status == "UNSAT" and cake_lpr == "s VERIFIED UNSAT"
#   (load() and finalize()); any other cake verdict gives status UNSAT_UNCHECKED and the cube stays open.
# - SKIP status (--skip) also counts a cube as closed for the frontier; I never pass --skip,
#   so no SKIP records can appear in my runs.
# - leaf cubes are top cube + split sub-cubes (literals over F's variables, relative to the case
#   CNF = F + case units); a cube is never treated as closed by a prefix.
# - top.icnf: when I pass --top, the file is march_cu CASE.cnf -d 7 -o top.icnf run by my
#   wrapper on the same case CNF (the driver's own march would write the same file:
#   it writes the header with nc+0 clauses and the same body); its sha is in leaves.jsonl.
# - liveness only (AUDIT NOTE-1): a march_cu "a 0" result makes the child equal its parent.
#
